{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082440Z_dev-02_flat_7c79", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No, the two thresholds differ.\n\n**dSph gamma-ray limits:** The one-sided 95% CL upper limit is set where 2[ln L_max − ln L(⟨σv⟩_95)] = 2.71. This is a TS drop of 2.71, or 1.355 in ln L. The nuisance parameter profiled over is the J-factor normalization of each dwarf, J = s·J0. It is profiled over log10 s in [−3, 3] with a Gaussian penalty whose width is the quoted σ_J on log10 J, taken from stellar kinematics.\n\n**AMS-02 antiproton limits:** The upper limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = −2 ln L. This is the nominal 95% two-sided interval threshold for one parameter. The paper says it differs from the usual one-sided 95% prescription with threshold 2.71. The nuisance parameter profiled over is the diffusive-halo half-height L. It is profiled over 1 ≤ L/kpc ≤ 12 with a Gaussian penalty in log10 L, centred on 4.96 kpc with σ(log10 L) = 0.197.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "turns": 2, "seconds": 7.795, "tool_calls": 1, "tool_result_chars": 147086, "input_tokens": 6, "output_tokens": 734, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 67415, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:24:48+00:00"}
